  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A particle is oscillating on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis with an amplitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> about the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math> with a frequency. A concave mirror of focal length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is placed at the origin (see figure).</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ce281efe-8aa9-40d6-a4f0-6187b0bdb05a-image.png\" style=\"width: 290px; height: 149px;\" /><br />Identify the correct statements?<br />(i) The image executes periodic motion.<br />(ii) The image executes non-periodic motion.<br />(iii) The turning points of the image are asymmetric with respect to the image of the point at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math>.<br />(iv) The distance between the turning points of the oscillation of the image is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>21</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "GfskL",
      "text": "(ii, iii)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
